  - a list of dicts (e.g., [{"item":"A", "amount": 10}, ...]) — column is the dict key
  - a list of lists/tuples (e.g., [(id, val), ...]) — column is an integer index
  - a dict mapping labels -> numeric values (e.g., {"A": 10, "B": 20}) — column ignored
  - a simple list of numbers — column can be None or ignored
- The function returns (stats_dict, matplotlib.figure.Figure)

