    and convert the text encoding. If OCR fails or yields no text, fall back to reading
    image comments (EXIF UserComment, PNG text chunks, JPEG comment).

    Parameters:
    - image_path (str): path to the image file.
    - src_encoding (str|'auto'): source encoding of raw bytes text; 'auto' attempts detection.
    - dst_encoding (str): target encoding for the returned bytes when return_bytes=True.
    - return_bytes (bool): if True, return bytes encoded with dst_encoding; otherwise return a Python str.
    - ocr_lang (str|None): language code(s) to pass to OCR engine (e.g., 'eng'). Only used by fallback pytesseract.
    - verbose (bool): if True, prints debug/warning messages.

    Returns:
    - str or bytes: extracted text (unicode string by default, bytes if return_bytes=True).

